WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:02.996
- [Narrator] This is the Roadster,

00:00:02.996 --> 00:00:04.090
(Roadster whooshing)

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:07.000
the first car Tesla ever released in 2008

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.584
and it was developed and
produced in California.

00:00:09.584 --> 00:00:11.340
(upbeat music)
(tape whirring)

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.970
Fast forward 13 years to today

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.620
and you can find Teslas on
the road around the world.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:17.460
- I think we're close

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.670
to establishing a Tesla
presence in Russia.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.810
- [Narrator] But Tesla isn't
just selling cars abroad,

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.270
it's also setting up
factories around the world.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.780
- The key for Tesla's global expansion

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:32.010
is going to be expanding
manufacturing capacity quickly.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.370
- [Narrator] Tesla's push comes at a time

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.580
when the stakes of going global are big

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.960
as the EV market will surge 775%

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.970
to about 35 million cars by 2030

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.944
and that can come with pitfalls.

00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:45.780
(woman shouting in foreign language)

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.060
- [Narrator] After a spate
of bad publicity in China,

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.160
Tesla sales took a hit in April

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.140
and auto analysts aren't
sure if the company

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.460
can keep growing as fast

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.880
in one of its biggest markets.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.120
- I think what Tesla's trying to do

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.970
is really drive home that
first-mover advantage,

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.623
make sure it retains that number one spot.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.550
- [Narrator] We analyzed
three key speeches by Musk

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.050
in the past year to
understand how Tesla plans

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.810
to put more of its vehicles on the road

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.221
all over the world.

00:01:11.221 --> 00:01:14.270
(upbeat music)

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.850
First, we go to Moscow.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.300
In May, Musk gave a speech
via video conference

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.400
to hundreds of students

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.500
and tech entrepreneurs
at a forum sponsored

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.800
by the Russian government.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.040
He spoke about a wide range

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.060
of topics from politics and religion

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.230
to outer space.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.920
- We need to establish
a self-sustaining base

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.900
on the moon and up on Mars.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.160
- [Narrator] But what
really made headlines

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.610
was when he hinted at future plans

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.090
for a new factory.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:41.000
- We're building one in
Texas, Nevada, California

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:45.190
and over time, we will
look to have factories

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:46.728
in other parts of the world

00:01:46.728 --> 00:01:48.847
but potentially Russia at some point.

00:01:48.847 --> 00:01:50.712
- [Narrator] The suggestion
came as a surprise

00:01:50.712 --> 00:01:53.560
because Tesla hasn't
sold many cars in Russia.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:56.660
There are around 700
vehicles on the roads there.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.360
But Russia could fit a
template Tesla has used before,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.153
to open factories where
it sees market potential.

00:02:02.153 --> 00:02:05.880
- There are two big electric
vehicle markets in the world:

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:06.713
China and Europe.

00:02:06.713 --> 00:02:08.620
Tesla's already in China

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.873
and now it's opening up plants in Europe.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.180
- [Narrator] That new plant is near Berlin

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:16.750
and auto analysts expect
it to open in early 2022.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:19.430
It's planning to produce
half a million cars a year

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.940
and this would allow Tesla
to directly sell its vehicles

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.280
to European countries

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.610
instead of importing them
from China and the US

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.130
as it currently does.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:28.970
With the three biggest markets covered,

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.360
auto analysts have been divided

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.631
over where Musk will set up shop next.

00:02:32.631 --> 00:02:34.330
Some say he should double down

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.770
on the so-called BRIC countries.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.220
- Brazil, Russia, India and China,

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.840
the big automakers are in Brazil

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.800
because that's a big market.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.940
It's probably a good guess

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.600
that Tesla's looking at that.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.560
- [Narrator] And of course, one of them

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.490
is the untapped market of Russia,

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:54.010
which grew by 95% last year.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.882
- I think there's a lot of talent

00:02:56.882 --> 00:02:57.932
and energy in Russia.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.160
- [Narrator] Building
factories in new countries

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.860
is a major logistical challenge,

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:05.920
especially with a hands-on
CEO like Elon Musk.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.230
- The big thing for Tesla right now

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.403
is the Giga Berlin, so it's in Berlin.

00:03:11.403 --> 00:03:13.930
I've spent a fair bit of time
in Berlin working on that.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.110
- [Narrator] In a one-on-one video call

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.820
with The Wall Street
Journal's editor in chief

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.045
in December last year,

00:03:18.045 --> 00:03:20.190
Musk explained how he
liked working closely

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:21.400
with his engineers.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.700
- When I have spent too much
time in a conference room,

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.090
that's generally when
things have gone awry

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:27.110
and when I go to spend
time on the factory floor,

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:30.800
we're really using the cars,

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.640
that's where things have gone better.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.130
- [Narrator] Musk says
being on the factory floor

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.330
is essential to creating good products,

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.810
especially because his
company builds many parts,

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:41.660
like the battery packs and develops much

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.180
of the software in house.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.850
But this makes it difficult for Tesla

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:45.890
to ramp up production,

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:47.610
compared with traditional automakers

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.299
that are moving into EVs.

00:03:49.299 --> 00:03:50.623
- It doesn't have the factories,

00:03:50.623 --> 00:03:53.751
it doesn't have the distribution
networks on the ground.

00:03:53.751 --> 00:03:57.570
Existing manufacturers like
Volkswagen, Toyota, GM,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.790
they already have a global
manufacturing footprint

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.550
and they already have global
distribution networks.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.170
So what they're doing

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:09.603
is converting existing plants
into electric vehicle plants.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.590
- [Narrator] Plus building
a factory from scratch

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.440
can cost billions of dollars.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.480
And if the company fails
to scale quickly enough

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.640
before other EVs flood the market,

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:20.810
a solution may be to think

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:23.150
more like a traditional automaker.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.600
- It may be able to do this
by building its own factories

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.180
or it may one day have to rely
on contract manufacturers,

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:32.980
like Foxconn, which builds for Apple,

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.271
and is now getting into electric vehicles.

00:04:36.271 --> 00:04:37.560
(upbeat music)

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:38.750
- [Narrator] Working in new markets

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:42.000
also means navigating different
regulatory environments.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.750
And in the US, Musk has been known

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.547
to collide with regulators.

00:04:45.547 --> 00:04:46.380
- But the best thing
that government can do

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:47.670
is just get out of the way.

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:51.270
- [Narrator] It's a contrast
to his public persona in China.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.970
- I'm very confident
that the future in China

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.160
is gonna be great.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.840
And that China is headed towards
being the biggest economy

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:58.230
in the world.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.060
- [Narrator] In March, Musk
sat down for an interview

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.850
with China's national television channel

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.100
to talk about the country's economic plan.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.490
- What attracts me most
about China's five-year plan

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.270
is the tremendous commitment

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.020
to a low-carbon economy

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.560
and ultimately, to a
sustainable energy economy.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.610
♪ That I would go anywhere for you. ♪

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:16.810
- [Trefor] That says a lot
about how he's been willing

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.210
to change his approach
when working in China.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.160
- I really wanna thank
the government officials

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.470
that have been really helpful.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.610
- [Trefor] Conflict with the authorities

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.240
really doesn't work here at all.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.217
He obviously knows that

00:05:26.217 --> 00:05:28.720
and has really done everything he can

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.980
to praise officials, to
praise the Chinese system.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:32.813
- [Narrator] Tesla has taken

00:05:32.813 --> 00:05:34.930
a conciliatory approach when challenged.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.630
For instance, at the
Shanghai Auto Show in April,

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.750
a woman climbed on top of a Tesla vehicle

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.938
to shout allegations about faulty brakes.

00:05:41.938 --> 00:05:44.550
(woman shouting in foreign language)

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:45.383
- [Narrator] The woman's claims

00:05:45.383 --> 00:05:46.990
couldn't be verified independently

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.500
but complaints about Tesla spread

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.230
across the Chinese internet.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.800
The company publicly apologized

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.710
and pledged to set up a
customer satisfaction unit.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:57.480
A few months later, Tesla
complied with Chinese regulators

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.120
to address safety issues
with the software upgrade

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:03.478
in more than 285,000 vehicles.

00:06:03.478 --> 00:06:06.620
Musk has been less contentious
with Chinese officials

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:07.720
and that has played a part

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.360
in Tesla's success there.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.700
For example, the factory in
Shanghai was built in 10 months.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:15.150
Just compare that with
his plant in Berlin.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:16.580
As far back as 2015,

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.510
Musk has courted German officials.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.950
Even the country's head
of state, Angela Merkel.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.560
But the plant is still
facing a six-month delay.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.530
Some industry watchers say it was caused

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.590
by Tesla's own lack of coordination,

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:29.900
given the company had
benefited from legislation

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:32.560
that helped to fast track construction.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.100
Musk has said German bureaucracy

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:35.920
and activists' environmental concerns

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:38.020
over water usage and the plant's impact

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:41.330
on local wildlife are why
the project is behind.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.960
He tweeted that the factory
wouldn't use as much water

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.350
and that trees in the area
were originally planted

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:47.843
to be turned into cardboard.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.360
The delay of the Berlin plant shows

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.400
how even a superstar CEO

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.860
can't get around German
approval processes.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.700
- It's still organized
kind of like a startup

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.520
with a charismatic leader

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.100
who basically controls
everything from the top down,

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.340
which makes it very hard

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:09.300
for a company to deal with
local regulatory issues.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.680
It needs strong management on the ground,

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.340
which it doesn't really have here.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:16.560
Maybe it needs a CEO and a real board.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:17.850
That could, in the long run,

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:20.283
hinder Tesla on its path to growth.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.350
- [Narrator] So if Elon Musk wants

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:24.910
to convert Tesla into
a truly global player,

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.050
the billionaire CEO may have to buckle up

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.352
and prepare for a bumpy ride.

00:07:28.352 --> 00:07:30.935
(upbeat music)

